ref('gelfandfuchs1968circle','Gel{\\cprime}fand, Israel M. and Fuchs, Dmitry B.','The cohomologies of the {Lie} algebra of the vector fields in a circle',1968,'https://www.mathnet.ru/eng/faa2800',journal='Functional Analysis and Its Applications',volume=2,number=4,pages='342--343',doi='10.1007/BF01075687',annote='Math-Net metadata and full two-page Russian original opened. Theorem 1 and degree-two cocycle read. Received 5 July 1968. The continuous smooth-vector-field cohomology is distinguished from an unrestricted algebraic cochain complex.')
ref('feiginfuchs1982invariant','Feigin, Boris L. and Fuchs, Dmitry B.','Invariant skew-symmetric differential operators on the line and {Verma} modules over the {Virasoro} algebra',1982,'https://www.mathnet.ru/eng/faa1619',journal='Functional Analysis and Its Applications',volume=16,number=2,pages='114--126',doi='10.1007/BF01081626',annote='Full Russian original47--63 opened; sections3.1--3.3, Theorem3.1, Proposition3.1 and section4 checked. Received15September1981; Russian issue2 of1982 predates September talk. Receipt is not treated as a public preprint date. Confirms minus1 in h and plus(c-13) in Phi. Not used as direct source for a bosonic oscillator formula.')
ref('neretin1983highest','Neretin, Yuri A.','Unitary representations with highest weight of the group of diffeomorphisms of a circle',1983,'https://mat.univie.ac.at/~neretin/papers/highest.pdf',journal='Functional Analysis and Its Applications',volume=17,number=3,pages='235--237',doi='10.1007/BF01078115',annote='Author-hosted three-page original opened. Theorem2 explicit bosonic operators and h=(alpha squared+beta squared)/2,c=1+12beta squared checked; older Chodos--Thorn construction cited there. Historical priority before1982 is indirect, not claimed read in the1974 original.')
talk(566,'1982-09-27','D. B. Fuchs','P001040-P001043','Virasoro Verma modules and semi-infinite exterior powers',r'The actual entry occupies P001041--P001042. Fuchs presents the central extension of circle vector fields, Verma modules, tensor-density modules and their semi-infinite exterior powers, then the Kac determinant criterion and a second oscillator construction. The explicitly cited Feigin--Fuchs paper had appeared in the second issue of 1982. The notebook reverses two signs, omits commutator factors, and writes operators which are not the required Heisenberg modes; these defects are separated from the valid representation-theoretic content.')
add(566,'The Witt algebra and its one-dimensional central extension','P001041','definition',r'\([e_i,e_j]=(j-i)e_{i+j}\), and the central correction at \(i+j=0\) is \((j^3-j)z/12\). The extension is called unique.',r'The Laurent-polynomial vector fields \(e_i=z^{i+1}\partial_z\) have the displayed bracket. Up to rescaling the central generator and equivalence, there is one nontrivial one-dimensional central extension, the Virasoro algebra. For smooth circle vector fields one uses continuous Lie-algebra cochains; uniqueness excludes the split extension.',r'The degree-two class is in \citet[Theorem~1]{gelfandfuchs1968circle} (1968); the exact mode convention appears in \citet[Section~3.1]{feiginfuchs1982invariant}.',('gelfandfuchs1968circle','feiginfuchs1982invariant'),verification='read the result',match='exact',reconstruction='Nontriviality, equivalence and the continuous-cochain qualification are supplied.')
add(566,'Verma modules, PBW basis and partition-number dimensions','P001041','construction',r'The vacuum satisfies \(e_{-1}v=e_{-2}v=0,\ e_0v=hv,\ zv=cv\); the ordered positive-mode monomials are required to be a basis.',r'The induced Verma module \(V_{h,c}\) has basis \(e_{i_1}\cdots e_{i_k}v\), \(i_1\ge\cdots\ge i_k>0\). Its level-\(n\) dimension is the partition number \(p(n)\), hence graded character \(\prod_{m\ge1}(1-q^m)^{-1}\). Since \(e_{-1},e_{-2}\) generate the negative subalgebra, their annihilation conditions imply every \(e_{-j}v=0\).',r'\citet[Section~3.1]{feiginfuchs1982invariant} gives this exact convention and universal property before the talk.',('feiginfuchs1982invariant',),literal='correct',verification='read the result',match='exact',reconstruction='The PBW basis condition is essential: a highest-weight quotient alone need not be a Verma module.')
add(566,'Tensor densities with two parameters','P001041','construction',r'\(e_if_j=[j+\mu-(i+1)\lambda]f_{i+j}\), interpreted as \(f_j=z^{j+\mu}(dz)^{-\lambda}\).',r'The Lie derivative of a density of weight \(-\lambda\) gives \(e_i(z^{j+\mu}(dz)^{-\lambda})=[j+\mu-(i+1)\lambda]z^{i+j+\mu}(dz)^{-\lambda}\). For nonintegral \(\mu\), this is an algebraic Laurent module or a density with monodromy, not necessarily an ordinary single-valued function on the circle.',r'The exact algebraic module is defined in \citet[Section~2.1]{feiginfuchs1982invariant}; the displayed action can also be verified directly by the Lie-derivative rule.',('feiginfuchs1982invariant',),verification='read the result',match='exact',reconstruction='The meaning of a nonintegral exponent is made explicit.')
add(566,'Semi-infinite wedges and normal-ordering of the zero mode','P001041-P001042','construction',r'Take wedges differing finitely from \(\cdots\wedge f_{-3}\wedge f_{-2}\wedge f_{-1}\). Nonzero modes act by a finite surviving sum, but the naive zero-mode sum diverges; the notes set \(e_0=[e_{-1},e_1]\) and compare \([e_{-2},e_2]\).',r'Fix the charge-zero tail. For \(i\ne0\), repeated factors make all but finitely many Leibniz terms vanish. The Virasoro relations require \(e_0=\tfrac12[e_{-1},e_1]\) and \(z=2([e_{-2},e_2]-4e_0)\). The central scalar records the finite discrepancy after regularizing the divergent diagonal sum.',r'\citet[Section~3.3, Proposition~3.1]{feiginfuchs1982invariant} supplies the exact wedge construction. The commutator coefficients follow directly from the notebook algebra.',('feiginfuchs1982invariant',),literal='false as written',verification='read the result',match='exact',reconstruction='Charge, regularization and the missing factors are explicit.')
add(566,'Highest weight and central charge of the wedge representation','P001042','theorem',r'The notebook has \(e_0=h+n\), \(h=\tfrac12\mu(\mu-2\lambda+1)\), followed by a question mark.',r'For the stated tail ending at \(f_{-1}\), the normal-ordered wedge module has \(h=\tfrac12\mu(\mu-2\lambda-1)\) and \(c=-2(6\lambda^2+6\lambda+1)\); a vector of level \(n\) has eigenvalue \(h+n\). Other charge sectors replace \(\mu\) by \(\mu+\text{charge}\).',r'These constants are printed in \citet[Section~3.3, Proposition~3.1, Russian p.~59]{feiginfuchs1982invariant}. The notebook sign is a faithful mathematical error, already marked doubtful by the recorder.',('feiginfuchs1982invariant',),literal='false as written',verification='read the result',match='exact',reconstruction='The omitted central charge is restored from the explicitly cited paper and the tail convention fixes the sign.')
add(566,'When the wedge realization is a Verma module','P001042','claim',r'\ru{Если неприводим, то явл. модулем Верма}.',r'If the charge-zero wedge module is irreducible, its nonzero vacuum generates it. The universal highest-weight map from \(V_{h,c}\) is then surjective, and both level-\(n\) spaces have dimension \(p(n)\); it is an isomorphism. Without irreducibility or cyclicity, equal characters alone do not make the canonical map an isomorphism.',r'The equal-character comparison and canonical map are in \citet[Section~3.3, pp.~59--60]{feiginfuchs1982invariant}. The short proof supplied here spells out the notebook inference.',('feiginfuchs1982invariant',),literal='correct',verification='read the result',match='exact',reconstruction='The universal-map and graded-dimension argument is written explicitly.')
add(566,'The reducibility locus of Virasoro Verma modules','P001042','question',r'Kac is credited with the criterion \(\Phi_{r,s}(h,c)=0\) for positive integers \(r,s\), but both factors use a minus sign before \((c-13)\).',r'Choose \(t\in\mathbb C^\times\) with \(c=13-6(t+t^{-1})\). Then \(V_{h,c}\) is reducible exactly when \(h=h_{r,s}(t)=((rt-s)^2-(t-1)^2)/(4t)\) for some \(r,s\ge1\). The first singular-vector level is the least \(rs\) giving the weight. The determinant at level \(n\) has factors \((h-h_{r,s})^{p(n-rs)}\), up to a nonzero normalization.',r'Kac announced the result in 1979; \citet[Theorem~3.1 and Section~4]{feiginfuchs1982invariant} states the determinant and supplies a proof before this talk. The polynomial printed there has plus signs before \((c-13)\).',('feiginfuchs1982invariant',),literal='false as written',verification='read the result',match='exact',problem='GP-1982-03',reconstruction='The parameterized form avoids the notebook polynomial sign error and makes the first-level qualification precise.')
add(566,'The central-charge-zero specialization','P001042','claim',r'\(c=0\Rightarrow h=(m^2-1)/24\).',r'At \(c=0\), take \(t=3/2\). Reducible highest weights are exactly \(((3r-2s)^2-1)/24\), \(r,s>0\), equivalently \((m^2-1)/24\) with \(m\in\mathbb Z\). The assertion describes reducibility, not every allowed highest weight at \(c=0\).',r'This is direct substitution in the criterion of \citet[Theorem~3.1]{feiginfuchs1982invariant}. Every integer is \(3r-2s\) with positive \(r,s\) after adding a sufficiently large multiple of \((2,3)\).',('feiginfuchs1982invariant',),verification='read the result',match='exact',reconstruction='The missing condition and integer range are supplied; the arithmetic equivalence is checked here.')
add(566,'Bosonic polynomial realization and the incorrect printed modes','P001042','construction',r'The second construction sets \(F_k=\sum_i x_i\partial_{x_{i+k}}\) and builds quadratic \(e_i\), with coefficient \(\alpha=\mu-i(\lambda+\tfrac12)\).',r'For a corrected oscillator realization, let \([a_m,a_n]=m\delta_{m+n,0}\), \(a_n=n\partial_{x_n}\), \(a_{-n}=x_n\) for \(n>0\), and \(a_0=p\). Then \(L_n=\tfrac12\sum_k:a_{n-k}a_k:-Q(n+1)a_n\) has \(c=1-12Q^2\), \(h=\tfrac12p(p-2Q)\). Relabel \(e_i=L_{-i}\) to match the notes. The printed \(F_k\) annihilate the constant polynomial for every \(k\), so cannot satisfy a nonzero Heisenberg central bracket.',r'The background-charge bosonic construction predates the talk through the older work cited by \citet[Theorem~2]{neretin1983highest}; that 1983 paper gives explicit corrected operators. Priority is verified indirectly, while the printed failure and the normalized replacement can be checked algebraically.',('neretin1983highest',),literal='false as written',verification='indirect',match='partial',reconstruction='The displayed normalized Heisenberg realization is a replacement, not a transcription correction. It is not attributed directly to the semi-infinite-wedge formula in Feigin--Fuchs.',confidence='medium')
problems.append(dict(id='GP-1982-03',title='Reducibility and first singular vectors of Virasoro Verma modules',statement=r'Determine all pairs \((h,c)\) for which the complex Virasoro Verma module is reducible, and the least positive level of a singular vector.',occurrences=['1982-566.7'],status=r'As of November 2026, solved before the September 1982 talk by the Kac determinant criterion, with a proof in Feigin--Fuchs (1982). Later appearances in this year reuse this identifier.',status_date='2026-11',refs=['feiginfuchs1982invariant']))
corr('P001042','Zero-mode commutators at the top of the page',r'\(e_0=[e_{-1},e_1]\), and comparison with \([e_{-2},e_2]\).',r'\([e_{-1},e_1]=2e_0\), \([e_{-2},e_2]=4e_0+z/2\).','Scan1042 inspected; substitute indices in the exact bracket on1041.')
corr('P001042','Highest weight following the Feigin--Fuchs reference',r'\(h=\mu(\mu-2\lambda+1)/2\).',r'\(h=\mu(\mu-2\lambda-1)/2\) for the stated charge-zero tail.','Scan1042 visibly has +1 and a question mark. Feigin--Fuchs1982 Proposition3.1 Russian p59 has -1 in this exact convention.')
corr('P001042','Equation (11), determinant factors',r'Minus \((c-13)(k_i^2-1)/24\) in both factors.',r'Plus \((c-13)(k_i^2-1)/24\) in both factors.','Scan1042 checked; Feigin--Fuchs1982 Theorem3.1 Russian p58 prints plus. At c0, r1,s2, the corrected factor has root h0, agreeing with the level2 singular vector.')
corr('P001042','Equations (14)--(16), purported oscillator realization',r'\(F_k=\sum_i x_i\partial_{x_{i+k}}\) used as the quadratic construction modes.',r'Use actual multiplication/differentiation Heisenberg modes and specify zero-mode, normal ordering and background-charge coefficient consistently.','Scan1042 checked. Every written F_k kills1, so their commutator on1 is0 and cannot equal a nonzero scalar; Neretin1983 Theorem2 gives an independently printed oscillator construction.')
audit.append('## Record 566\nActual pages1041--1042. Russian read; scan1042 inspected in full for both commutators, doubtful h sign, determinant signs and F_k formula. Opened Gelfand--Fuchs1968 Math-Net metadata and full2-page Russian PDF: Theorem1 and degree2 cocycle. Opened Feigin--Fuchs1982 full17-page Russian PDF, especially sections3.1--3.3 and4; read Theorem3.1, Proposition3.1. Receipt15Sep1981 distinguished from publication issue2 of1982; no unverified preprint date. Kac1979 priority is stated in their introduction, not certified by reading the original Kac lecture. Neretin1983 author PDF opened, Theorem2 checked; Chodos--Thorn priority indirect. Direct checks: e0 factors, vacuum tail sign, c0 parameterization and all-integer3r-2s, printed F_k cannot be Heisenberg. Previous index searched for Virasoro/Verma/Kac determinant: no exact problem ID found. Reserve GP-1982-03 for recurrence in573.')
